# shed_blue -- generated by tools/cad/build_shells.py from tools/cad/shells/. DO NOT EDIT.
# blue-roofed utility shed by the helipad: 4.5 x 3.5, gable roof, real eave
# 5.5 x 4.2 m footprint, 3.2 m tall. One piece per material group, all at the
# building's own origin: `tex NAME TILE` is per model file, so a wall and a roof cannot
# share one. The y on each line is the height that group was drawn at, put back: model.c
# rebases every OBJ's lowest vertex to zero, which would otherwise land the roof on the
# ground. Hand-placed extras, if any, follow at the bottom from
# tools/cad/shells/extras/shed_blue.part
piece models/own/shell/shed_blue_floor.obj   0 0.000 0   1 1 1   0 0 0   0.860 0.860 0.930  tex concrete_rough 0.7
piece models/own/shell/shed_blue_wall.obj   0 0.120 0   1 1 1   0 0 0   1.670 1.730 1.830  tex plaster_smooth 0.9
piece models/own/shell/shed_blue_trim.obj   0 2.280 0   1 1 1   0 0 0   0.350 1.220 1.420  tex corrugated 1
piece models/own/shell/shed_blue_roof.obj   0 2.420 0   1 1 1   0 0 0   0.460 1.600 1.820  tex corrugated 1
piece models/own/shell/shed_blue_metal.obj   0 2.120 0   1 1 1   0 0 0   0.580 0.590 0.650  tex concrete_rough 0.8

# The kit's frames, seated IN the reveals the shell cuts: each piece is pushed back
# into the wall by its own architrave projection, so the moulding finishes flush with
# the plaster instead of standing on it. Generated from the same Walls calls that cut
# the holes, so a frame and its reveal cannot drift apart.
piece models/own/arch/plain_door.obj   0.000 0.120 -1.690   1.000 1.000 1.000   0.0 0.0 0.0   1.470 1.250 0.880  tex planks_weathered 2
piece models/own/arch/window_small.obj   2.197 1.020 0.000   0.750 0.750 0.750   -90.0 0.0 0.0   1.670 1.730 1.830  tex plaster_smooth 0.9

# ---- from tools/cad/shells/extras/shed_blue.part ----
# Hand-placed, not part of the fabric: four corner battens, the one bit of the old box-and-wedge
# shed_blue.part that wasn't either a wall, a roof, an opening or a step -- kept for the cheap
# vertical shadow line they give the corners. Positioned just inside the new wall's own corners
# (half-width 2.25, half-depth 1.75) and rising from the plinth to the wall top.
piece models/shapes/box.obj  2.20  0.12  1.70  0.15 2.30 0.15  0 0 0  1.47 1.25 0.88  tex planks_weathered 2.0
piece models/shapes/box.obj  2.20  0.12 -1.70  0.15 2.30 0.15  0 0 0  1.47 1.25 0.88  tex planks_weathered 2.0
piece models/shapes/box.obj -2.20  0.12  1.70  0.15 2.30 0.15  0 0 0  1.47 1.25 0.88  tex planks_weathered 2.0
piece models/shapes/box.obj -2.20  0.12 -1.70  0.15 2.30 0.15  0 0 0  1.47 1.25 0.88  tex planks_weathered 2.0
